      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 \u7dca mg. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects.\n\nI suspect a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and daily totals. These are some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum.\n- **850 mg twice daily**, which is 1,700 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into doses of about 565 mg.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose at a different frequency.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you intended. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed it. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
