       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is double the maximum labeled dose, and metformin has no added benefit above about 2,550 mg/day. The risks of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity do go up at that dose. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. You also haven't given a clinical reason for the higher dose, so I can't treat this as a deliberate exception.\n\nHere's what I can do right away:\n- Enter **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum).\n- Enter a lower dose or a different schedule that you choose.\n- Enter the order with a note for pharmacy review, if you give me the dose you intend and your rationale.\n\nIf you still need 1,700 mg three times daily, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. It would then need to go through your hospital's dose-override process.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
